var tafsirData_76 = {
  "1": "\"Is there not a period of time when each human is nothing yet worth mentioning?\" opens Surah al-Insan with humility, echoing the previous proof that you were a sperm-drop, then a clot, then perfected male and female, and the question is such a Creator unable.\n\n“Is there not a period of time when each human is nothing yet worth mentioning?” translates “hal ata ‘ala al-insani hinun mina al-dahri lam yakun shay’an madhkura,” has there come upon man a time when he was not a thing remembered. Period of time, or “hinun mina al-dahri,” is an era, a stretch, like the smooth earth’s long ages, the seven heavens’ creation, and the flood that overflowed where We carried you in the Ark. Nothing yet worth mentioning indicates that before the drop, before the plant-like growth from earth, you were not named, not addressed, not detested, not honoured, not even a sperm-drop.\n\nThis follows the fingertip restoration and both sexes proof to deepen humility. You were nothing, then a drop, then a clot, then perfected, so resurrection is even easier, as with the Pen, the Record well-preserved, and the presentation where no secret stays hidden. Your nothingness before mention shows that being something is a gift, as is hearing, sight, and intellect you hardly thank, and being dispersed over earth and gathered.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to read nothing worth mentioning as worthlessness. It is origin humility, not worthlessness, as with the Blessed in Whose Hands rests all authority created death and life to test which is best in deeds, so worth is earned through best deeds, not claimed like honour that expels inferior.\n\nFor reflection, remember the period when you were nothing. That memory cures the halu‘ impatience distressed with evil and withholding with good, the hunger for more despite abundant wealth and children, and the stubbornness with revelations. It should make you grateful, in awe without seeing, and willing to fulfil vows and fear a Day of sweeping horror, giving food despite desire to the poor, orphan, and captive for the sake of Allah, seeking neither reward nor thanks, fearing the horribly distressful Day, so nothing becomes something held in honour in Gardens where fruit is easy to reach.",
  "2": "\"˹For˺ indeed, We ˹alone˺ created humans from a drop of mixed fluids, ˹in order˺ to test them, so We made them hear and see.\" gives the creation, purpose, and equipment after the nothing period. The verse is foundational.\n\n“For indeed, We alone created humans from a drop of mixed fluids, in order to test them, so We made them hear and see” translates “inna khalaqna al-insana min nutfatin amshajin nabtalihi fa-ja‘alnahu sami‘an basira.” We alone emphasizes that no idol like Wadd, no powerless force instead of the Most Compassionate, did this. Drop of mixed fluids, or “nutfatin amshajin,” is the sperm-drop mixed, the same nutfah that becomes ‘alaqah then perfected, causing growth like a plant, spread earth, and spacious pathways. It is the mixed drop that the denier who asks mockingly “When is the Day?” forgets when he loves fleeting and neglects Hereafter.\n\nIn order to test them, or “nabtalihi,” is the purpose, as with death and life created to test which is best, with abundant rain as test, with wealth and children as test, and with the garden as test. Test explains why hearing and seeing are given right after. So We made them hear and see indicates that faculties are for testing, not for boasting, as with hearing, sight, and intellect you hardly thank and the Pen.\n\nHear and see are the tools to listen and reason so you are not among residents of Blaze who lament if only we had listened and reasoned, and to walk upright, not crawl facedown.\n\nThis follows nothing worth mentioning to show that something worth mentioning, a hearing, seeing tested human, is a gift.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think Test excuses impatience. Impatience is the test’s material; the excepted who pray consistently, give rightful share, and are properly observant show it can be passed.\n\nFor practice, use hearing and seeing to show the Way, to be grateful or ungrateful as next states, to fulfil vows, fear the sweeping horror, and give food despite desire, so test becomes Garden and silk, radiance and joy, where you neither see scorching heat nor bitter cold, and Garden shade is right above with fruit easy to reach.",
  "3": "\"We already showed them the Way, whether they ˹choose to˺ be grateful or ungrateful.\" states guidance after creation to test. The Way is made clear.\n\n“We already showed them the Way, whether they choose to be grateful or ungrateful” translates “inna hadaynahu al-sabila imma shakiran wa imma kafura,” We guided him to the path, either grateful or ungrateful. Showed the Way, or “hadayna al-sabila,” is like the balance so people may administer justice, the Light that brings from darkness, the Reminder that would humble a mountain, the Pen, the weighty revelation recited properly, and the spacious pathways earth was spread for. Way here is the Straight Path walked upright, not crawling facedown.\n\nGrateful or ungrateful, or “shakiran wa kafura,” is the same division as believers vs disbelievers He created you yet some disbelieve while some believe, submitted vs deviant fuel for Hell, righteous vs less so among jinn, and those in awe without seeing vs those who not. Grateful is the one who uses hearing and seeing to thank, to fulfil vows, fear the sweeping horror, give food for Allah’s sake seeking neither reward nor thanks, and fears the horribly distressful Day.\n\nThis follows created from mixed drop to test, hearing and seeing, to show that test is not without guidance.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to read “We showed the Way” as forcing gratitude. Showing is offering, as with “let whoever wills take the Right Way” and “whoever wills be mindful, but they cannot unless Allah wills, He is worthy to be feared and entitled to forgive.”\n\nFor reflection, you have been shown the Way that the jinn called amazing leading to Right Guidance so we believed. Choose grateful, not ungrateful. Grateful leads to chains, shackles, and blazing Fire being for the ungrateful disbelievers, while grateful leads to camphor drink, spring where servants drink flowing at will, radiance, joy, Garden and silk, as next details, so the Way shown becomes the Garden’s shade right above and fruit easy to reach.",
  "4": "\"Indeed, We have prepared for the disbelievers chains, shackles, and a blazing Fire.\" states the preparation for the ungrateful choice after showing the Way. The recompense is ready.\n\n“Indeed, We have prepared for the disbelievers chains, shackles, and a blazing Fire” translates “inna a‘tadna li-l-kafirina salasil wa aghlalan wa sa‘ira,” chains, fetters, and blaze, as with the raging Flame that rips scalps, Saqar that does not let live, scorching skin, overseen by nineteen, the difficult Day far from easy, and the overwhelming punishment for turning from remembrance. Prepared, or “a‘tadna,” indicates readiness, as with shackles, raging Fire, choking food in store, dunes of shifting sand, and the severe punishment prepared.\n\nDisbelievers, or “kafirin,” are the ungrateful, the kafura, who were shown the Way but chose ungratefulness, who were created to test but withheld when touched with good, who loved fleeting and neglected Hereafter, whose faces will be gloomy anticipating devastation, and who are among the wicked asked what landed you in Hell, not praying, not feeding poor.\n\nChains, shackles, blazing Fire are the opposite of the virtuous drink flavoured with camphor from a flowing spring, radiance, joy, and Garden and silk for the grateful.\n\nThis follows showed the Way, grateful or ungrateful, to show that ungrateful has a prepared destination.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to hear chains as metaphor for regret only. Chains are real, as with feet tied in shroud and chains seventy arms long.\n\nFor the living who have a period when they were nothing, then a drop, then hearing and seeing, and who have been shown the Way, choose grateful now, before the soul reaches collar bones and no healer saves, before woe and more woe, so prepared for disbelievers is not your preparation, but the Gardens held in honour prepared for the virtuous who fulfil vows and fear the sweeping horror.",
  "5": "\"Indeed, the virtuous will have a drink ˹of pure wine˺—flavoured with camphor—\" promises the grateful’s drink after the disbelievers’ chains. The contrast is immediate.\n\n“Indeed, the virtuous will have a drink of pure wine—flavoured with camphor—” translates “inna al-abrara yashrabuna min ka’sin kana mizajuha kafura,” the righteous, the dutiful, drink from a cup mixed with camphor. Virtuous, or “abrar,” are the grateful, the good, the dutiful, who fulfil vows, fear the sweeping horror, give food despite desire to poor, orphan, captive for Allah’s sake, fear the distressful Day, and are delivered, granted radiance and joy, rewarded with Garden and silk, not the halu‘ withholding, not the luxury deniers, not the spooked zebras fleeing reminder.\n\nDrink of pure wine flavoured with camphor is the opposite of choking food and blazing Fire, of pus that only evildoers eat, and of hamim. Camphor, or “kafur,” is cool, fragrant, as with ginger and Salsabil also among Garden drinks, and as with the camphor spring flowing at will next.\n\nCup, or “ka’s,” is the vessel as with the crystal cups filled precisely as desired, the pen and what everyone writes, the well-preserved Record.\n\nThis follows chains for disbelievers to show two prepared destinations, as with residents of Fire not equal residents of Paradise, and submitted not wicked.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think virtuous drink is worldly wine. It does not let live or die, it does not intoxicate, it is flavoured with camphor and flows at will, grants radiance.\n\nFor practice, be virtuous now, show Way by being grateful, fulfil vows, fear the sweeping horror, give food while desiring it, fear the horribly distressful Day, so the drink flavoured with camphor becomes your drink, the spring flowing at will becomes your spring, and the blazing Fire’s chains are not yours.\n\nExtra: Camphor, or “kafur,” also recalls the coolness of the Gardens where never seeing scorching heat or bitter cold is the climate. Camphor’s cool balances ginger’s warmth later, showing that the Gardens’ drinks are tempered, not the raging Flame that rips scalps or the choking food. For the virtuous who were nothing then a drop for test, shown the Way, and chose grateful, the camphor drink is the first taste of the spring flowing at will, where the distressful Day’s horror is replaced by radiance and joy, and where the chain of seventy arms is replaced by crystal cups filled precisely as desired.",
  "6": "\"˹from˺ a spring where Allah’s servants will drink, flowing at their will.\" details the source of the camphor drink for the virtuous. The spring is personal and pliable.\n\n“from a spring where Allah’s servants will drink, flowing at their will” translates “‘aynan yashrabu biha ‘ibadu Allahi yufajjirunaha tafjira,” a spring from which the servants of Allah drink, causing it to gush forth abundantly. Servants of Allah, or “‘ibad Allah,” are the virtuous, the grateful, the mindful who protect families, the submitted who sought right course, the excepted who pray, and the people of the right, not the deviant fuel for Hell. Spring, or “‘ayn,” is like the spring flowing at will, the abundant rain showered, the gardens and rivers supplied, and the rivers of Gardens under which rivers flow for ever and ever.\n\nFlowing at their will indicates control, as with wealth that does not merely circulate among rich but flows as rightful share, and as with the Pen’s writing at will. The servants cause it to gush, showing honour, not just reception.\n\nThis follows camphor drink to show that the flavour is not bottled, but spring-sourced, fresh, like the flowing water that will be brought if yours sinks.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to treat spring as mythic. It is the excellent provision granted to those who believe and do good, the Gardens under rivers, the splendid homes, the elevated Garden where fruit hangs within reach.\n\nFor the living who were nothing then a drop, then hearing and seeing, shown the Way, choose grateful, fulfil vows, give food despite desire, so the spring where servants drink gushing at will becomes your spring, and the chains, shackles, blazing Fire remain the disbelievers’ preparation, not yours, and your shroud’s tied feet become Garden’s silk.\n\nMore: Flow at will, or “yufajjirunaha tafjira,” also shows that the servants’ will is aligned with Allah’s will, as with “you cannot will unless Allah wills, Indeed All-Knowing, All-Wise,” and “He is worthy to be feared and entitled to forgive.” Flowing at will is not arbitrary, but honoured, like the provision from sources never imagined and the ease after hardship. For the grateful, flowing at will is the reward for devoting yourself wholeheartedly and taking Him alone as Trustee, so will becomes the Garden’s easy fruit and the spring’s abundant gushing, not the hard purpose of garden owners fixated on excluding poor.",
  "7": "\"They ˹are those who˺ fulfil ˹their˺ vows and fear a Day of sweeping horror,\" defines the virtuous who drink the camphor spring. The traits are vow and fear.\n\n“They are those who fulfil their vows and fear a Day of sweeping horror” translates the virtuous, the grateful, the servants. Fulfil their vows, or “yufuna bi-al-nadhr,” keep their pledges, vows, as with true to trusts and covenants, honest in testimony, the pledge of believing women not to associate, steal, fornicate, kill children, falsely attribute, nor disobey in what is right, and the covenant to hear and obey. Fear a Day of sweeping horror, or “yakhafuna yawman kana sharruhu mustatira,” fear a Day whose evil is widespread, as with the Day sky molten brass, mountains wool, no close friend asks, wicked wish to ransom with everyone, raging Flame ripping scalps, earth and mountains shaking, sky splitting, children’s hair grey, and souls at collar bones.\n\nSweeping horror, or “mustatir,” is extensive, spreading, like the garden’s ashes while they slept and the dunes of shifting sand. Fear here is mushfiq awe, like those in awe without seeing with mighty reward, those who fear punishment knowing none should feel secure.\n\nThis follows spring flowing at will to show who drinks from it.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to limit vows to formal oaths, like despicable vain oath-taker. Vows here are sincere pledges to Allah and people, as with making room, lending good loan, protecting families.\n\nFor practice, fulfil vows now, fear the sweeping horror Day now, so you are delivered from its horror, granted radiance and joy, and rewarded with Garden and silk, where horror is replaced by radiance, sweeping is replaced by Garden’s shade right above, and fear becomes the bright faces looking at their Lord, not the gloomy anticipating devastation.\n\nFurther: Vows and sweeping horror also link to the midnight vow of the garden owners to harvest all early, whose horror was the garden reduced to ashes while they slept, and to the luxury deniers indulging until they face their Day. Fulfilling vows contrasts with leaving no thought for Allah’s Will, and fearing the sweeping horror contrasts with feeling secure that One in heaven will not swallow or unleash stones. To fulfil vows now, be true to trusts and covenants, honest in testimony, and properly observant, so vow becomes the good sent forth found with Allah better and greater, and sweeping horror becomes the deliverance with radiance and joy.",
  "8": "\"and give food—despite their desire for it—to the poor, the orphan, and the captive,\" details the virtuous act that fulfils vows and fears the sweeping horror. The giving is sacrificial.\n\n“and give food—despite their desire for it—to the poor, the orphan, and the captive” translates the virtuous feeding. Give food despite desire, or love for it, is to feed while themselves needing or desiring, as with helpers who preferred emigrants despite need and were saved from selfishness and are truly successful, with the rightful share to the asker and deprived, and with letting the poor enter your garden today. Poor, or “miskin,” the needy; orphan, or “yatim,” the parentless; captive, or “asir,” the prisoner, even if disbeliever, showing mercy beyond kin, as with places of worship only for Allah yet kindly fair dealing with those who neither fight nor drive you out.\n\nThis follows fulfil vows and fear a Day to show that fear appears as feeding despite desire, not as gloom that anticipates devastation, but as action.\n\nGive food despite desire contrasts with withholding when touched with good, gathering and hoarding that the Flame summons, and the despicable withholder of good, transgressor, evildoer, brute.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to limit feeding to surplus. Despite desire indicates while loving food, as with the garden owners who loved harvest, yet virtuous give.\n\nFor the one who was nothing, then a drop, then hearing and seeing, shown the Way, grateful vs ungrateful, this feeding chooses grateful, so the Day of sweeping horror is delivered from, radiance and joy granted, and the Garden’s shade right above and fruit easy to reach becomes yours, where feeding despite desire in days gone by becomes eating and drinking joyfully.\n\nExtra: Despite their desire for it also measures sincerity, as with the helpers who preferred emigrants despite need and were saved from selfishness and are truly successful. Despite desire indicates the food given is loved, not surplus, like the garden’s fruit that was loved but withheld, and the merchandise fanfare that drew crowds. Giving despite desire is the practical form of “We feed you only for Allah, seeking neither reward nor thanks,” and of fearing the horribly distressful Day. For the tested drop, shown the Way, feeding despite desire chooses grateful, so the poor, orphan, and captive are fed, and the Day’s horror is delivered from, and the Garden’s shade right above becomes yours.",
  "9": "\"˹saying to themselves,˺ “We feed you only for the sake of Allah, seeking neither reward nor thanks from you.\" reveals the virtuous’ inner motive while giving food despite desire. The speech is internal, sincere.\n\n“saying to themselves, ‘We feed you only for the sake of Allah, seeking neither reward nor thanks from you’” translates the virtuous’ intention. Only for the sake of Allah, or “li-wajhi Allah,” for His Face, His pleasure, as with the Lord in Whose Hands rests all authority, Most Capable, who is with you wherever you are. Seeking neither reward nor thanks from you distinguishes divine reward from human repayment, as with the good loan multiplied and forgiven by the Most Appreciative, Most Forbearing, not by people, and as with “We will be in Gardens held in honour” where honour is from Allah, not from those fed.\n\nThis follows giving food despite desire to show that giving is not for show like worthless planks impressive speech that impresses, not for powerless force help, not for merchandise better than what is with Allah, but for the Lord.\n\nSaying to themselves indicates they may not utter it aloud to avoid reminding the poor of favour, like not expecting more in return, not doing favour to seek increase. It is sincere, opposite to the despicable who expects more.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think seeking no thanks means coldness. No thanks sought from people, but thanks is sought from Allah, the Most Appreciative who multiplies.\n\nFor practice, give food despite desire, even while over-occupied by day, and intend only for Allah’s sake, as with the helpers’ love, the sincere repentance that perfects light, and the night worship more impactful, so feeding becomes the radiance and joy, Garden and silk, that Allah will deliver from the horribly distressful Day they feared, where reward is better and greater with Him.",
  "10": "\"We fear from our Lord a horribly distressful Day.”\" voices the virtuous’ fear that motivates feeding despite desire and fulfilling vows. The fear is specific.\n\n“We fear from our Lord a horribly distressful Day” translates “inna nakhafu min rabbina yawman ‘abusan qamtarira,” we fear from our Lord a Day frowning, grim, distressful. ‘Abusan qamtarira is a Day that frowns, scowls, spreads distress, as with the Day sky molten brass, mountains wool, no close friend asks, soul at collar bones, feet tied, driven to your Lord, difficult Day far from easy for disbelievers, and the Day children’s hair grey. Horribly distressful captures the severity that even the garden reduced to ashes while they slept and the Fire that does not let live only hint at.\n\nFear from our Lord, not from powerless forces, idols, or wealth that says ancient fables, shows proper object, the Lord of east and west, King, Holy, Most Capable, whose Hands hold authority.\n\nThis follows “We feed you only for Allah, seeking neither reward nor thanks” to show that seeking only Allah includes fearing His Day, as with those who fear punishment knowing none should feel secure, and those in awe without seeing with mighty reward.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to hear fear as despair that forgets that He is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful, worthy to be feared and entitled to forgive, who accepts repentance and provides from sources never imagined.\n\nFor the one who was nothing, then a drop for test, shown the Way, grateful or ungrateful, fear should make you grateful, fulfilling vows, giving food, so fear becomes deliverance, radiance, joy, Garden and silk, reclining on couches, never seeing scorching heat or bitter cold, shade right above, fruit easy, silver vessels, crystal cups, and ginger drink, where horribly distressful Day is not yours but for those who indulged and amused until they faced their Day.",
  "11": "\"So Allah will deliver them from the horror of that Day, and grant them radiance and joy,\" states the divine response to the virtuous who fulfil vows, fear the sweeping horror, and feed despite desire for Allah’s sake fearing the distressful Day.\n\n“So Allah will deliver them from the horror of that Day, and grant them radiance and joy” translates the recompense. Deliver, or “waqahum,” is to protect, shield, as with protecting yourselves and families from Fire whose fuel is people and stones, and as with the Ark carried when floodwater overflowed as reminder for attentive ears. Horror of that Day, or “sharra dhalika al-yawm,” is the sweeping, distressful Day they feared, the Day sky like molten brass, mountains wool, no helper, scales ripping, and the Day children’s hair grey, sky split, promise fulfilled. Grant them radiance, or “nadrah,” brightness on faces, and joy, or “surura,” happiness in hearts, as with bright faces looking at their Lord, radiance and joy opposite to eyes downcast covered with disgrace, faces gloomy, and woe and more woe.\n\nThis follows fearing to show that fear is answered with deliverance, as with the way out for the mindful and sufficient for those who put trust.\n\nRadiance and joy are the inner and outer light perfected, as with “Our Lord, perfect our light for us and forgive us, You are Most Capable of everything,” and the light that shines ahead and to the right for those who believe and lend good loans.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think deliverance is automatic without vow, fear, and feeding. Deliverance follows those traits, as with the exception of people of the right not detained.\n\nFor the human created from mixed drop to test, made hear and see, shown the Way, this verse shows which Way leads to delivery, grateful, not ungrateful. Be among the grateful who fulfil, fear, and feed, so deliverance is yours, and radiance and joy replace the raging Flame that summons the distressed withholding and the gloomy anticipation.",
  "12": "\"and reward them for their perseverance with a Garden ˹in Paradise˺ and ˹garments of˺ silk.\" details the reward after deliverance, radiance, and joy. Perseverance is the cause.\n\n“and reward them for their perseverance with a Garden in Paradise and garments of silk” translates “wa jazahum bi-ma sabaru jannatan wa harira,” He will reward them for patience, a Garden and silk. Perseverance, or “sabarum,” is patience beautified, as with beautiful patience commanded, not like Jonah in distress, and as with persevere for your Lord after shunning idols, and as with those who pray consistently and are properly observant. Perseverance includes fulfilling vows, fearing the sweeping horror, giving food despite desire, and feeding for Allah alone while over-occupied by day and standing half the night reciting properly.\n\nGarden and silk are the recompense, the Garden in Paradise, the elevated Garden where fruit hangs within reach, where they recline on canopied couches, never seeing scorching heat or bitter cold, shade right above, fruit easy, silver vessels, crystal cups, ginger, and Salsabil. Silk, or “harir,” is the garment of honour, as with never-ending reward and outstanding character, the Gardens held in honour, and the splendid homes, opposite to shackles and the Fire’s scorching skin.\n\nThis follows radiance and joy to show that inner deliverance becomes outer Garden and clothing.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to treat perseverance as mere endurance of hardship, like the garden owners’ fixated purpose. Perseverance here is for Allah, for the horribly distressful Day, with vows kept and food given.\n\nFor the one who was nothing worth mentioning, then a drop to test, who was shown grateful or ungrateful, perseverance chooses grateful, so reward is Garden and silk, where perseverance’s hardship while desiring food becomes the ease of silver vessels precisely filled as desired, and the Garden’s shade right above where you never see scorching heat.",
  "13": "\"There they will be reclining on ˹canopied˺ couches, never seeing scorching heat or bitter cold.\" describes the Garden’s repose after perseverance rewarded with Garden and silk. The posture and climate are perfect.\n\n“There they will be reclining on canopied couches, never seeing scorching heat or bitter cold” translates the Garden’s rest. Reclining, or “muttaki’ina fiha ‘ala al-ara’ik,” is to lean, rest on couches, as with the people of the right reclining face to face, held in honour, whose Gardens are elevated, fruit easy. Canopied couches are high, adorned, like the Pen’s writing and the Throne borne, showing honour, not worthless planks leaned.\n\nNever seeing scorching heat nor bitter cold, or “la yarawna fiha shamsan wa la zamhariran,” neither sun nor bitter cold, indicates climate moderation, neither the scorching heat of the raging Flame that rips scalps, the Fire that does not let live, nor the biting cold of zamharir opposite heat, as with the Fire’s two extremes, and the dunes of shifting sand. It is the opposite of the Day earth and mountains shake and sky splits, where heat and cold would be felt.\n\nThis follows Garden and silk to detail Garden interior, and precedes shade right above and fruit easy.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to read never seeing sun as darkness. No scorching heat indicates perfect shade, not darkness, as with extended shade for the people of the right and the Garden’s shade right above.\n\nFor the one created from mixed drop, shown the Way, grateful or ungrateful, reclining in Garden is the end of grateful. To recline there, be among the grateful who fulfil vows, fear the sweeping horror, feed despite desire, and fear the distressful Day, so perseverance becomes reclining, and the Day’s horror becomes deliverance with radiance and joy, where scorching and bitter cold are never seen and the Pen writes your reclining as honour.",
  "14": "\"The Garden’s shade will be right above them, and its fruit will be made very easy to reach.\" details proximity of shade and fruit for those reclining on canopied couches. The Garden is designed for ease.\n\n“The Garden’s shade will be right above them, and its fruit will be made very easy to reach” translates that the Garden’s shade is near, and its fruits are made low, easy, as with the elevated Garden whose fruit hangs within reach, where they are told to eat and drink joyfully, and the excellent provision for ever and ever. Shade right above indicates continual, gentle shade, not the raging Flame’s heat or zamharir cold just negated, and not the swallowing earth or unleashed stones, but the extended shade for the people of the right and the shade that is never out of season. Fruit very easy to reach, or “dhullilat qutufuha tadhilan,” is humbled, lowered, at will, as with the spring flowing at their will and the crystal silver filled precisely as desired.\n\nThis follows reclining never seeing heat or cold to show that reclining is not distant from provision; shade and fruit come to you, as with being waited on with silver vessels.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think shade right above is oppressive. It is mercy, as with the smoothed earth you move upon, now shaded.\n\nFor the grateful who were nothing, then a drop for test, shown Way, fulfilled vows, fed despite desire, shade right above is the answer to fearing the sweeping horror’s exposure, and easy fruit is the answer to hunger for more.\n\nPractice by giving shade and easy fruit now, making room when told, letting the poor enter your garden today, providing according to means, so Garden’s shade right above becomes your shade, and the difficult Day far from easy becomes your reclining, where the Fire’s choking food is not yours but the Garden’s easy fruit.",
  "15": "\"They will be waited on with silver vessels and cups of crystal—\" describes the service in the Garden after shade and fruit. The vessels are precious and precise.\n\n“They will be waited on with silver vessels and cups of crystal—” translates the service, as with being waited on with silver vessels and crystal cups, the Pen and what everyone writes, the well-preserved Record, and the attentive service for the grateful. Silver vessels, or “aniyah min fiddah,” and cups of crystal, or “akwab kana qawarira,” are clear, shining, as with crystal, not earthenware, indicating honour, like the gardens held in honour and the splendid homes.\n\nWaited on indicates honour, as with the Garden’s near fruit and shade, where you do not need to rise from canopied couches to fetch; service comes to you, as with the Pen writing for you and the Trustee sufficient.\n\nThis follows shade and fruit to add drink service, and precedes crystalline silver, filled precisely as desired, and ginger drink and Salsabil.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to reduce this to luxury for its own sake, like the luxury deniers left to Me for a little while. Silver here is not hoarded and gathered wealth that the Flame summons, but honour, as with the never-ending reward and outstanding character.\n\nFor the grateful who were nothing, drop, hearing and seeing, Way shown, fulfilled vows, fed despite desire for Allah’s sake, fearing distressful Day, delivered with radiance and joy, rewarded with Garden and silk, reclining, shade, fruit, the silver vessels are the recompense for perseverance, where perseverance included not doing favour expecting more, and shunning idols, and purifying garments, so service is pure.\n\nMore: Silver vessels and crystal cups also echo the Pen and what everyone writes, the well-preserved Record, and the attentive service for the grateful who were wrapped and stood half the night. Waited on indicates honour, as with the Garden’s near fruit and shade where you do not rise from couches. Silver here is not hoarded wealth that the Flame summons, but honour, as with outstanding character and Gardens held in honour. For the grateful, silver vessels are the recompense for not doing favour expecting more and for shunning idols, so service is pure and the difficult Day far from easy becomes easy, and the raging Fire’s shackles are not yours.",
  "16": "\"crystalline silver, filled precisely as desired.\" qualifies the silver vessels and crystal cups just mentioned. The description is of substance and measure.\n\n“crystalline silver, filled precisely as desired” translates “qawarira min fiddatin qaddaruha taq dira,” crystal of silver, they measured it precisely. Qawarira min fiddatin is an oxymoron, crystal clear yet silver white, indicating a unique, luminous material, not earthly silver that tarnishes nor crystal that shatters, but a heavenly blend, like camphor and ginger drinks, Salsabil, and the Gardens’ silk. Filled precisely as desired, or “qaddaruha taq dira,” they measured it with precise determination, as with the Pen that writes and determines, the well-preserved Record, and the appointed time that never delays.\n\nPrecisely as desired indicates that the serving is not random, not the garden reduced to ashes while they slept, not the choking food and painful punishment in store, but exact, as desired, like the spring flowing at their will and the fruit made very easy to reach.\n\nThis follows silver vessels and crystal cups to define their nature, and precedes ginger drink, showing that the drink service is measured.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to treat crystalline silver as earthly luxury to be hoarded and gathered. It is measured, desired, not hoarded, as with the good loan multiplied.\n\nFor the grateful, crystalline silver filled precisely is the reward for being true to trusts and honest in testimony, properly observant, where measurement is honour, not the despicable’s oath-taker or slanderer. For practice, measure your giving precisely as desired for the poor, the orphan, and the captive, not withholding when touched with good, so precise filling becomes your Garden’s precise cups, where you never see scorching heat or bitter cold and are waited on with honour.\n\nFurther: Crystalline silver, filled precisely as desired, also mirrors the precise measure of the Pen that writes every calamity or blessing before creation, the appointed time that never delays, and the provision according to means for waiting women. Precisely as desired shows that Garden service is not the garden reduced to ashes while they slept, not the choking food, but exact, as desired, like the spring flowing at will and the fruit made very easy to reach. For the grateful, precise filling is the reward for being true to trusts and honest in testimony, where measurement is honour, not the despicable oath-taker’s vain measure. Measure your giving precisely for the poor, orphan, captive, so precise becomes your Garden’s cups.",
  "17": "\"And they will be given a drink ˹of pure wine˺ flavoured with ginger\" adds another drink after camphor and crystalline silver. The variety shows honour.\n\n“And they will be given a drink of pure wine flavoured with ginger” translates “wa yusqawna fiha ka’san kana mizajuha zanjabila,” they will be given to drink a cup mixed with ginger. Drink of pure wine, or “ka’s,” is the cup as with camphor drink and ginger drink, not the worldly wine that intoxicates, but the Garden’s pure wine that does not let live or die, scorching. Flavoured with ginger, or “zanjabil,” is warm, aromatic, as with camphor’s cool, showing balance, not scorching heat or bitter cold, but perfect.\n\nThis follows crystalline silver precisely filled to show that after the precise crystal, a new flavour is offered, and precedes from a spring called Salsabil, indicating source, as with the spring flowing at will.\n\nGinger’s warmth contrasts with camphor’s cool, both within the Garden where never seeing scorching heat or bitter cold is the climate, showing that flavours are for delight, not for harm.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to equate ginger wine with worldly intoxicant, as the despicable’s withholder might. Garden wine is pure, like the Pen’s writing and the Record well-preserved, not the ancient fables.\n\nFor the virtuous who were nothing, drop, test, Way shown, grateful, fulfilled vows, feared sweeping horror, fed despite desire for Allah alone fearing distressful Day, delivered, radiant, joyful, gardened, silk, reclining, shade, fruit, silver, crystal, the ginger drink is the next honour, where the spring Salsabil flows, and the Day’s horror is replaced by radiance, and where the grateful’s perseverance is rewarded beyond the fleeting world they did not love and the Hereafter they did not neglect but sought.\n\nMore: Ginger flavoured drink also balances camphor’s cool, showing that the Gardens’ drinks are tempered to neither scorching heat nor bitter cold, the climate where you never see either. Ginger’s warmth, or “zanjabil,” is aromatic, like camphor, and its spring Salsabil next shows source. For the virtuous who were nothing, drop, test, Way shown, grateful, fulfilled vows, feared sweeping horror, fed despite desire for Allah alone, delivered, radiant, gardened, silk, reclining, shade, fruit, silver, crystal, the ginger drink is the next honour, where Salsabil flows and the Day’s horror is replaced by joy, and perseverance is rewarded beyond the fleeting world they did not love.",
  "18": "\"from a spring there, called Salsabîl.\" names the source of the ginger drink just mentioned. Salsabil is a heavenly spring whose name suggests smooth, easy flow.\n\n“from a spring there, called Salsabil” translates the ginger cup’s source, “‘aynan fiha tusamma Salsabila,” a spring therein named Salsabil. There indicates the Garden where virtuous recline, never seeing scorching heat, shade above, fruit easy, silver vessels, crystal, ginger. Salsabil is the name of that spring, as with Tasnim and Kafur, indicating a distinct, flavoured source, like the spring flowing at will where servants drink. The name’s root suggests “ask for a way,” smooth passage, showing the drink flows gently at will, precisely filled, never choking like the choking food and painful punishment in store for luxury deniers.\n\nThis follows ginger drink to show its origin, and precedes eternal youths, bliss and vast kingdom, silk and bracelets, and the Lord will give them a pure drink.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to treat Salsabil as earthly river to be searched for on maps like the garden reduced to ashes while they slept. It is a heavenly spring, the excellent provision granted to those who believe and do good, whose rivers flow under Gardens.\n\nFor the one who was nothing then a drop for test, shown the Way, grateful, fulfilled vows, fed despite desire, feared the distressful Day, delivered, radiant, Garden and silk, reclining, shade, fruit, silver, crystal, ginger, Salsabil is the next honour, where the Day’s horror is replaced by ease, and the weighty revelation soon sent is now the light that is tasted as pure wine, and the Pen has written your perseverance as Garden and Salsabil, not as dunes and shackles.\n\nExtra: Salsabil also contrasts with the choking food and painful punishment in store for luxury deniers left to Me for a little while. Salsabil’s smooth, easy flow is the opposite of choking, and its being called by name shows honour, like the spring flowing at will where servants drink. For the virtuous who fulfil vows, fear sweeping horror, give food despite desire for Allah alone, and fear the distressful Day, Salsabil is the reward for perseverance with Garden and silk, where the distressful Day’s horror is delivered from and radiance and joy replace gloom.",
  "19": "\"They will be waited on by eternal youths. If you saw them, you would think they were scattered pearls.\" describes the servers in the Garden after Salsabil. The servers are perpetually youthful.\n\n“They will be waited on by eternal youths. If you saw them, you would think they were scattered pearls” translates the service, “wa yatufu ‘alayhim wildanun mukhalladun idha ra’aytahum hasibtahum lu’lu’an manthura,” immortal youths circulate among them, when you see them you think they are scattered pearls. Eternal youths, or “wildan mukhalladun,” are created to serve, never aging, like scattered pearls for beauty and precision, as with crystal silver filled precisely and fruit made very easy. Waited on indicates honour, as with silver vessels and shade right above, where you do not rise from couches to fetch.\n\nScattered pearls, or “lu’lu’an manthura,” indicates beauty, cleanliness, and spread, opposite to the worthless planks leaned, the impressive appearance that impressed but was plank-like, and the despicable withholder. Pearls scattered show abundance and order, like the Pen and what everyone writes.\n\nThis follows Salsabil to add service, and precedes bliss and vast kingdom, silk and bracelets.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to treat eternal youths as exploited. They are honoured servants created for this, as with the Pen’s writing and the Record well-preserved, not the withholder’s hoarding.\n\nFor the grateful who were nothing, drop, test, Way shown, fulfilled vows, fed despite desire, their service by eternal youths is the reward for making room when told, for preferring emigrants despite need, and for giving rightful share, where service that you gave becomes service you receive, amplified by the Most Appreciative, Most Forbearing who multiplies the good loan.\n\nMore: Scattered pearls also contrast with the worthless planks leaned that impress like the despicable oath-taker, and with the garden reduced to ashes. Pearls scattered show that service in the Garden is abundant, not hoarded like wealth gathered and hoarded that the Flame summons. The youths as pearls indicate that even the servers are beautiful, not the brute’s snout marked, and not the eyes downcast covered with disgrace, but bright and scattered with order. To be waited on by them, be among the grateful who give food despite desire and fear the horribly distressful Day, so scattered pearls become your servers, not the shackles that bind.",
  "20": "\"And if you looked around, you would see ˹indescribable˺ bliss and a vast kingdom.\" invites the gaze to wander in the Garden after eternal youths as scattered pearls. The view is overwhelming.\n\n“And if you looked around, you would see indescribable bliss and a vast kingdom” translates “wa idha ra’ayta thamma ra’ayta na‘iman wa mulkan kabira,” when you look there, you see delight and great kingdom. Bliss, or “na‘im,” is the same Gardens of Bliss promised to the righteous, the life of bliss after knowing reckoning, and the Gardens of Bliss with their Lord. Vast kingdom, or “mulkan kabira,” is great dominion, like the Blessed in Whose Hands rests all authority and He is Most Capable, the kingdom that is His and all praise is for Him, and honour belonging to Allah, His Messenger, and believers, not the honour that expels inferior.\n\nLooked around indicates that wherever you look in the Garden, bliss and kingdom appear, not a single cup or couch, but an expanse, opposite to the garden reduced to ashes where they looked and said “We lost our way.”\n\nThis follows eternal youths to show that service is within a kingdom, and precedes garments of fine green silk and silver bracelets and pure drink from the Lord.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to hear vast kingdom as metaphor for feeling. It is a real dominion granted, as with the better garden hoped for after turning, made real.\n\nFor the one who was nothing worth mentioning, then a drop to test, shown grateful or ungrateful, this vast kingdom is for the grateful who chose grateful, whose striving has been appreciated, as next states. To see bliss and kingdom, fulfil vows, fear the sweeping horror, give food despite desire for Allah alone, and fear the distressful Day, so looking around in the Garden is your reward, not the raging Flame that rips scalps where no kingdom is.",
  "21": "\"The virtuous will be ˹dressed˺ in garments of fine green silk and rich brocade, and adorned with bracelets of silver, and their Lord will give them a pure drink.\" details clothing and final drink after bliss and vast kingdom. The garments signify honour.\n\n“The virtuous will be dressed in garments of fine green silk and rich brocade, and adorned with bracelets of silver, and their Lord will give them a pure drink” translates the dressing. Fine green silk, or “sundus,” is the inner, delicate silk; rich brocade, or “istabraq,” is the outer, heavy silk, together the Garden and silk promised for perseverance, opposite to the shackles, raging Fire, and choking food for luxury deniers. Bracelets of silver, or “asawira min fiddah,” are ornaments, like the silver vessels and crystal cups precisely filled, indicating honour, not hoarded wealth that the Flame summons. The Lord will give them a pure drink, or “sharaban tahura,” a purifying drink from the Lord Himself, beyond camphor, ginger, Salsabil, the purest, like the white, cool camphor and the warm ginger, now pure.\n\nThis follows bliss and vast kingdom to show that kingdom includes dress, and precedes “All this is surely a reward for you. Your striving has been appreciated,” which explains why.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to treat silk and bracelets as worldly extravagance that luxury deniers indulged in. For the virtuous who were nothing, drop, test, Way shown, grateful, fulfilled vows, fed despite desire, this silk is reward for perseverance, not indulgence.\n\nFor practice, be virtuous, persevere, and the garments you wore to be mindful to best ability, to hear and obey, to spend, become silk and silver, and the pure drink from your Lord replaces the choking food and the pus that only evildoers eat, and your vast kingdom remains as the Gardens held in honour where you are told to eat and drink joyfully.",
  "22": "\"˹And they will be told,˺ “All this is surely a reward for you. Your striving has been appreciated.”\" voices the divine acknowledgment after garments and pure drink. The announcement is personal.\n\n“And they will be told, ‘All this is surely a reward for you. Your striving has been appreciated’” translates the address to the virtuous. All this, or “hadha,” refers to the camphor drink, spring flowing at will, radiance, joy, Garden and silk, reclining, shade, fruit, silver vessels, crystal, ginger, Salsabil, eternal youths as scattered pearls, bliss and vast kingdom, fine silk, brocade, silver bracelets, and pure drink. Surely a reward for you indicates it is recompense for what you did in days gone by, for which you are told to eat and drink joyfully, and for which your striving has been appreciated, or “sa‘yakum mashkura,” your effort thanked.\n\nStriving appreciated echoes the Pen and what everyone writes, the good you send forth found with Allah better and greater, and the Most Appreciative, Most Forbearing who multiplies the good loan. Appreciated shows that the All-Aware who is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful, Most Appreciative, has noted every vow fulfilled, every sweeping horror feared, every meal given despite desire for His sake.\n\nThis follows garments and pure drink to explain why.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to hear reward as wage that obliges the Most Compassionate. Reward is favour He grants to whoever He wills, Lord of infinite bounty, yet He appreciates striving as if it were a loan.\n\nFor the human created from mixed drop to test, made hear and see, shown the Way grateful or ungrateful, this tells you striving appreciated is the path to vast kingdom. Strive as the wrapped who stands half the night reciting properly, remember wholeheartedly, take Trustee, and be among the grateful who feed despite desire, so striving appreciated becomes your “All this is surely a reward for you” on the Day bright faces look at their Lord, not gloomy anticipating devastation.",
  "23": "\"Indeed, it is We Who have revealed the Quran to you ˹O Prophet˺ in stages.\" addresses the Prophet after the virtuous’ reward and appreciated striving, returning to revelation. The verse affirms gradual descent.\n\n“Indeed, it is We Who have revealed the Quran to you O Prophet in stages” translates “inna nahnu nazzalna ‘alayka al-Qur’ana tanzila,” We sent down the Quran upon you in stages, as with the weighty revelation soon sent, the reminder to the whole world, the Light that brings from darkness, and the Pen. In stages, or “tanzila,” is gradual, measured, like the measured recitation tartil, half the night or less or more, recite what is easy, and the command descends between seven heavens so you may know He is Most Capable and encompasses all knowledge.\n\nWe Who have revealed emphasizes that the same We who created you from a drop, showed the Way, prepared chains and blazing Fire for the ungrateful and camphor springs for the grateful, is the revealer, not a poet or fortune-teller, not an idol like Wadd, not a powerless force.\n\nIn stages indicates wisdom, not to humble the Prophet with a mountain at once, but to train the community, as with flexibility for the sick, traveller, and fighter.\n\nThis follows your striving appreciated to show that striving was guided by staged revelation.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think stages imply imperfection. Stages are mercy, like the made very easy life for the one created alone, but here used for training, not for hunger for more.\n\nFor believers who will take the Right Way while you will, stages mean you can recite what is easy, establish prayer, pay alms, lend good loan, and seek forgiveness, so stages become your vast kingdom’s steps, and the Reminder that would humble a mountain remains your light perfected, not the choking food and painful punishment in store for luxury deniers.",
  "24": "\"So be patient with your Lord’s decree, and do not yield to any evildoer or ˹staunch˺ disbeliever from among them.\" commands patience after affirming staged revelation. The instruction balances endurance and resistance.\n\n“So be patient with your Lord’s decree, and do not yield to any evildoer or staunch disbeliever among them” translates “fa-sbir li-hukmi rabbika wa la tuti‘ minhum athiman aw kafura,” be patient for your Lord’s judgment and do not obey among them a sinful or ungrateful disbeliever. Patient with your Lord’s decree is the beautiful patience commanded, enduring denial with beautiful patience while they see the Day as far, not like Jonah in distress who would have been cast blameworthy without grace then chosen and made righteous. Lord’s decree, or “hukm,” includes determining day and night, knowing you are unable to maintain half the night, accepting repentance, reciting what is easy, and the weighty revelation.\n\nDo not yield to any evildoer or staunch disbeliever among them, or “athiman aw kafura,” is the same division as grateful vs ungrateful, submitted vs deviant fuel for Hell, and the despicable oath-taker, slanderer, gossip-monger, withholder, transgressor, brute. Athim is sinful, kafur is intensely ungrateful, both among the deniers who indulged and amused until they faced their Day.\n\nThis follows revelation in stages to show that staged revelation requires patience, not yielding.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to read patience as passivity, like monasticism invented. Patience here is active, remembering the Name morning and evening, prostrating part of night, glorifying long.\n\nFor the virtuous who were nothing, drop, test, Way shown, choose grateful and be patient with decree, not yielding to the ungrateful who would have you compromise so they would yield, or to the withholder who says do not spend, so patience becomes the Garden and silk, radiance and joy, where the difficult Day far from easy is not difficult for you.",
  "25": "\"˹Always˺ remember the Name of your Lord morning and evening,\" orders constant remembrance after commanding patience and not yielding. The timing is comprehensive.\n\n“Always remember the Name of your Lord morning and evening” translates “wa-dhkur isma rabbika bukratan wa asila,” remember the Name at dawn and dusk, as with remember the Name wholeheartedly and devote, take Him as Trustee of east and west, worship in the night more impactful, and over-occupied by day you have a long glorification. Morning and evening cover the day’s ends, like the two witnesses bearing true testimony, the sun as radiant lamp and moon as reflected light, and the points of sunrise and sunset whose Lord is truly capable to replace.\n\nAlways indicates both night standing half or less or more and day sabhan, so remembrance spans.\n\nThis follows patience and not yielding to show that patience is sustained by remembrance, not by wealth that says ancient fables.\n\nRemembering the Name morning and evening contrasts with loving fleeting world and neglecting a weighty Day ahead, and with indulging and amusing until they face their Day.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to limit remembrance to utterance. Remembrance includes reciting what is easy, establishing prayer, paying alms, lending good loan, and walking upright, all as the Pen writes.\n\nFor the one who was nothing worth mentioning, then a drop to test, made hear and see, shown grateful or ungrateful, remembering morning and evening chooses grateful, fulfilling vows, feeding despite desire for Allah alone, so remembrance becomes radiance and joy, Garden and silk, reclining, shade, fruit, silver, crystal, ginger, Salsabil, eternal youths, bliss and vast kingdom, fine silk, silver bracelets, and pure drink where striving is appreciated.\n\nFurther: Remembering morning and evening also counters loving fleeting world and neglecting a weighty Day ahead. Morning and evening remembrance is the opposite of indulge and amuse until they face their Day, and of rushing headlong to mock. Morning and evening, like points of sunrise and sunset whose Lord is truly capable, frame the day over-occupied with duties, making remembrance constant. For the one who was nothing, then a drop for test, shown grateful or ungrateful, remembering morning and evening chooses grateful, so the weighty Day ahead is not neglected but prepared for, and the vast kingdom and bliss remain, not the raging Flame that summons hoarders.",
  "26": "\"and prostrate before Him during part of the night, and glorify Him long at night.\" details night devotion after morning and evening remembrance. The night is for prostration and glorification.\n\n“and prostrate before Him during part of the night, and glorify Him long at night” translates the night worship that is more impactful and suitable for recitation, the wrapped standing half the night or less or more, reciting properly, and the Messenger standing for nearly two-thirds, half, or a third, as do some with him, determined by the One who determines day and night. Prostrate, or “sujud,” is the act they will be asked to do when the Shin is bared but cannot if they were called to prostrate when fully capable but chose not to, eyes downcast covered with disgrace. Glorify long at night is to praise, as with glorify the Name of your Lord, the Greatest, Blessed is the One in Whose Hands rests all authority, and the Lord of east and west to be taken as Trustee.\n\nDuring part of the night and long at night indicate that night prostration is not the whole night except a little, but a part, and glorification is long, like weighty revelation soon sent, the Reminder that would humble a mountain, and the Pen.\n\nThis follows morning and evening to complete the day-night cycle.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to think night glorification replaces the rightful share and feeding the poor. Night worship more impactful precisely because it fuels those day acts, making the grateful give food despite desire.\n\nFor the virtuous who fulfil vows and fear the sweeping horror, night prostration and long glorification are the training that makes the Day’s horror delivered from, and the radiance and joy granted, so the horribly distressful Day feared becomes the Day bright faces look at their Lord, not gloomy anticipating devastation, and the vast kingdom remains yours, appreciated striving.",
  "27": "\"Surely those ˹pagans˺ love this fleeting world, ˹totally˺ neglecting a weighty Day ahead of them.\" diagnoses the opponents after commanding morning, evening, and night worship. The contrast is stark.\n\n“Surely those pagans love this fleeting world, totally neglecting a weighty Day ahead of them” translates “inna ha’ula’i yuhibbuna al-‘ajilah wa yadharuna wara’ahum yawman thaqila,” they love the hasty world and leave behind them a heavy Day. Fleeting world, or “‘ajilah,” is the same love that made them withhold when touched with good, love merchandise better than what is with Allah, and love the hasty harvest without “Allah willing.” Neglecting a weighty Day, or “yawman thaqila,” is the same weighty as the weighty revelation soon sent, the difficult Day far from easy, the Inevitable Event, the Striking, the Day sky molten brass, mountains wool, no helper, where the wicked wish to ransom with everyone on earth. Thaqila is heavy, grave, as with saqar that does not let live, scorching skin, nineteen keepers.\n\nThis follows prostration and glorification at night to show that night worship is neglected by those who love fleeting.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to hear fleeting world only as wealth, not as the halu‘ impatience that loves the hasty and neglects the weighty. Lovely world includes honour that expels inferior, oaths as shields, and whisper to exclude poor.\n\nFor the one who was nothing, drop, hearing and seeing, shown grateful or ungrateful, loving fleeting chooses ungrateful and its chains, shackles, blazing Fire; loving the weighty Day chooses grateful and its camphor, Salsabil, radiance, Garden and silk. Choose to remember morning and evening, prostrate part of night, glorify long, so weighty Day ahead of them is not your weight, but your vast kingdom and bliss.\n\nMore: Fleeting world, or “‘ajilah,” also includes the garden’s early harvest, the caravan’s merchandise, the fanfare along with caravan that drew crowds from the pulpit, and honour that expels inferior. Fleeting is the hasty, as with halu‘ withholding when touched with good. Totally neglecting a weighty Day, or “wara’ahum yawman thaqila,” leaving behind them a heavy Day, is like leaving the Reminder that would humble a mountain, the weighty revelation soon sent, and the balance. Neglecting is leaving, as with leaving to Me the luxury deniers for a little while. To not neglect, take the Right Way now, remember morning and evening, prostrate part of night, glorify long, so fleeting becomes Gardens held in honour where you never see scorching heat.",
  "28": "\"It is We Who created them and perfected their ˹physical˺ form. But if We will, We can easily replace them with others.\" reminds of creation and capability after diagnosing love of fleeting and neglect of weighty Day. The verse is both affirmation and warning.\n\n“It is We Who created them and perfected their physical form. But if We will, We can easily replace them with others” translates the same as “He created you yet some are disbelievers while some are believers, and He is All-Seeing,” and the Lord of easts and wests truly capable to replace with better and cannot be prevented, and “Do you see any of them left alive?” after ‘Ad like palm trunks. Created them and perfected form, or “shaddadna asrahum,” We strengthened their structure, their build, as with He shaped you perfecting form, and the seven heavens without flaw. Perfected form indicates they are not weak, yet the One who perfected can replace.\n\nIf We will, We can easily replace them with others, or “badalna amthalihim tabdila,” We can substitute with likes of them in creation, showing the Pen can rewrite, the Record can enumerate, and the appointed time never delays.\n\nThis follows loving fleeting and neglecting weighty to show that the neglected weighty includes being replaced.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to hear replacement as threat to make you despair of the Most Appreciative, Most Forbearing who multiplies good loans. Replacement is for the ungrateful who persist, not for the grateful whose striving is appreciated.\n\nFor the grateful who were nothing, drop, hearing and seeing, Way shown, fulfilled vows, fed despite desire, replacement is not needed; you are already the better, the virtuous in Gardens held in honour, whose replacement would be worse. To remain, continue worshipping in night more impactful, remembering wholeheartedly, taking Trustee, so replacement is for the fleeting lovers, not for you.",
  "29": "\"Surely this is a reminder. So let whoever wills take the ˹Right˺ Way to their Lord.\" defines the whole passage as reminder and invites will, echoing earlier “Surely this is a reminder. So let whoever wills take the Right Way” after sky splitting and promise fulfilled, and after Hell as warning to humankind.\n\n“Surely this is a reminder. So let whoever wills take the Right Way to their Lord” translates that the preceding—from is there not a period when you were nothing, to created from mixed drop to test, hearing and seeing, Way shown grateful or ungrateful, chains and blazing Fire, camphor drink, Salsabil, vows, sweeping horror, feeding despite desire for Allah alone, distressful Day, deliverance, radiance, Garden and silk, shade, fruit, silver, crystal, ginger, eternal youths, bliss, kingdom, fine silk, silver bracelets, pure drink, striving appreciated, revelation in stages, patience, not yielding, morning and evening remembrance, night prostration, fleeting love, creation perfected and replaceable—is all tadhkirah, reminder, like the Ark for attentive ears, the mountain-humbling Quran, and the Reminder for the whole world.\n\nLet whoever wills take the Right Way indicates volition, as with lead or lag for the warning to humankind, every soul detained except people of the right, and you will be presented with no secret hidden. Right Way, or “sabilan ila rabbihi,” is the Straight Path walked upright, the Balance so people may administer justice, and the spacious pathways earth was spread for to walk.\n\nThis follows created and perfected, can replace, to show that the will to take the Right Way is the grateful choice that avoids replacement.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to read “whoever wills” as independent of Allah’s will, like the powerless force that would help instead of the Most Compassionate. The next verse clarifies “But you cannot will unless Allah wills, Indeed All-Knowing, All-Wise.”\n\nFor practice, will to take the Right Way now, remember morning and evening, prostrate part of night, glorify long, so willing becomes the lead that is Gardens held in honour, not the lag that is detained, and the reminder that is enough becomes your light perfected.",
  "30": "\"But you cannot will ˹to do so˺ unless Allah wills. Indeed, Allah is All-Knowing, All-Wise.\" balances the previous “let whoever wills take the Right Way” with divine will, knowledge, and wisdom.\n\n“But you cannot will to do so unless Allah wills. Indeed, Allah is All-Knowing, All-Wise” translates that willing is not isolated, as with “He is worthy to be feared and entitled to forgive” where He is worthy, and with the Lord of pathways’ planning flawless. Cannot will unless Allah wills shows that even the grateful choice to fulfil vows, fear the sweeping horror, and feed despite desire is enabled, as with the weighty revelation soon sent, the pen and what everyone writes, and the reminder to the whole world. All-Knowing, All-Wise parallels All-Knowing, All-Wise who descends command between seven heavens so you may know He is Most Capable and encompasses all knowledge, and the Most Subtle, All-Aware who knows whether you speak secretly or openly.\n\nIndeed, Allah is All-Knowing, All-Wise indicates that His will is not arbitrary, but knowing and wise, as with the test of best deeds, the abundant rain as test, and wealth and children as test but great reward with Him.\n\nThis follows let whoever wills to prevent boasting that taking the lead is self-made, like honour that expels inferior.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to use “unless Allah wills” as excuse to not try, as with feeling secure that One in heaven will not swallow. The Quran pairs it with “let whoever wills,” preserving both effort and reliance.\n\nFor the one who was nothing, drop, hearing and seeing, Way shown, grateful or ungrateful, willing the Right Way requires Allah’s will, so ask Him, devote wholeheartedly, take Trustee, and trust the Most Capable who holds all authority, so willing becomes the Gardens held in honour where striving is appreciated, and the ungrateful’s chains remain not yours.",
  "31": "\"He admits whoever He wills into His mercy. As for the wrongdoers, He has prepared for them a painful punishment.\" closes Surah al-Insan with mercy and prepared punishment, the two destinations shown throughout.\n\n“He admits whoever He wills into His mercy. As for the wrongdoers, He has prepared for them a painful punishment” translates the final division, as with submitted not wicked, Gardens vs raging Flame, bright vs gloomy, and every soul detained except people of the right. Admits into His mercy, or “yudkhilu man yasha’u fi rahmatihi,” is to enter into mercy, like delivering from horror, granting radiance and joy, rewarding with Garden and silk, reclining, shade, fruit, silver, crystal, ginger, Salsabil, eternal youths, bliss, kingdom, fine silk, silver bracelets, pure drink, and striving appreciated. Whoever He wills indicates favour He grants to whoever He wills, Lord of infinite bounty, but will is All-Knowing, All-Wise, not random, who admits the grateful who fulfilled vows, feared, fed, and feared again.\n\nAs for the wrongdoers, or “zalimin,” He has prepared for them a painful punishment, or “‘adhaban alima,” indicates readiness, as with chains, shackles, blazing Fire, shackles, raging Fire, choking food, dunes, stern grip for Pharaoh, and the Fire that does not let live.\n\nThis follows you cannot will unless Allah wills to show that admission into mercy is His will, but your will to take the Right Way aligns with it.\n\nA misunderstanding would be to read admission as favouritism that ignores best deeds test, where honour belongs to Allah. Admission respects best deeds, as with the Pen writing and the well-preserved Record.\n\nFor reflection, the period when you were nothing, then a drop for test, hearing and seeing, Way shown, grateful or ungrateful, now is the time to will the Right Way, so you are admitted into His mercy, not among wrongdoers for whom painful punishment is prepared, and your vast kingdom and bliss become your mercy, not your regret."
};